/-!
# Small coloring witnesses for the Hall--Janko Sylow involutions

These tables use the unchanged degree-100 ATLAS J2G1-p100B0 Sylow enumeration.
A coloring separates distinct commuting elements: four colors for the identity
and 2-central involutions, and eight in each outer involution centralizer.
`Checks` verifies coverage and separation in the kernel. The generator in
`source/generate.py` supplies witnesses only (original CFSG code, Apache 2.0).
Source: Aschbacher--Smith K.4.5, printed p.460.
-/

@[expose] public section
namespace CFSG.Quasithin.ChapterK.JankoTwo.InvolutionGeometry.Certificate
